Add a static-scale E4M3FN mode to the split-KV speculative verifier.

This patch is intentionally kernel-focused. It is applied after
spec-decode-attn.patch and spec-decode-int8-kv.patch. The FlashInfer runtime
dispatch is kept in a separate patch so the FP8 math can be validated against a
dequantized BF16 reference before changing backend routing.

vLLM's normal per-layer FP8 KV cache stores E4M3FN bytes plus one K and one V
scale for the layer. Triton on SM80 cannot lower a native NVIDIA fp8e4nv load,
so the verifier passes a zero-copy uint8 view and explicitly decodes E4M3FN
bits before BF16 tensor-core dot products:

    score = (q . decode_e4m3fn(k_bytes)) * k_scale
    value = (p * v_scale) . decode_e4m3fn(v_bytes)

The per-token-head INT8 path remains unchanged. STATIC_QUANT and QUANT are
mutually exclusive.

Apply with experimental/cmp170hx-mixed-fp8/install.sh after the normal patch
stack has been installed.

Written against the repository's vLLM 0.27.1 patch stack.

